    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d49-a7">

                <pb facs="0774" n="764" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv04/pg764"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-14">May 14th, 1919</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Telegram</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">General Dupont to Marshal Foch, Paris, and General Nudant,
                    Spa.</p>
                <p>No. 964. General Henrys telegraphs on the 12th May:— <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I learn that in Polish Silesia the Germans are in violation of the
                            conditions of peace requisitioning supplies of all kinds, viz. corn,
                            cattle, flour, etc., and are hastily sending back to Germany rolling
                            stock of railways. Great discontent and agitation of the population have
                            been caused thereby. Rising to be feared. I ask whether Germans are
                            justified or not in removing rolling stock from districts to be
                            evacuated and thus depriving entire province of material indispensable
                            to economic life. If not, I request steps may be taken to stop these
                            proceedings”.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>(Signed) <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">General
                    Dupont</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
